speechtext:
I venture to suggest to
the minister that first of all these matters should be dealt with by a bill. I have long felt that estimates of this kind should be dealt with as we deal with the appropriations for the commission in Ottawa and for the harbours of Halifax and Vancouver. These are advances made by the state to the railways;
I think a separate bill should be introduced and that, as far as possible, details in sums should be mentioned. I apprehend that a supply bill will be founded on these estimates; am I right in assuming that this will be a separate supply bill?
